From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:29:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: dwmac4: disable RBUE in the default channel
 interrupt mask

Since commit 1b9707e6f1a9 ("net: stmmac: enable RPS and RBU interrupts")
the receive buffer unavailable interrupt is enabled on every DMA
channel, so that rx_buf_unav_irq counts. It does nothing else:
dwmac4_dma_interrupt() counts RBU and schedules no NAPI for it.

When the page pool runs dry, the RX refill cannot hand descriptors back
to the DMA. The RX DMA suspends with RBU set, and RBU is raised again
right after it is cleared while frames keep arriving. In multi-MSI mode
(INTM = 1) the abnormal summary of a channel is signalled on the common
MAC interrupt, and stmmac_mac_interrupt() does not service
DMA_CHAN_STATUS, so the level line stays asserted and one CPU spends all
its time in the interrupt handler. The RX NAPI and the refill on that
CPU starve.

Seen on the Radxa Cubie A7S (Allwinner A733, dwmac 5.30) with failed RX
refills under RX load: the MAC interrupt line storms with RBU and AIS
set in the channel status, while the RX and TX queue lines are quiet.

The same storm was fixed for XGMAC2 by taking RBUE out of its default
mask, commit d3265c19b35d ("net: stmmac: xgmac2: disable RBUE in default
RX interrupt mask"). Do the same for dwmac4, for cores before and from
4.10 (only the A733 was tested). Recovering a dry ring is the job of the
refill path; this interrupt schedules nothing. rx_buf_unav_irq reads 0
from now on, as it did before 1b9707e6f1a9.

This is the minimal fix, as for XGMAC2. That stmmac_mac_interrupt() does
not service DMA_CHAN_STATUS in multi-MSI mode is a separate problem and
is left alone here.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with RX refills failed on purpose under RX
load, the MAC interrupt line stays quiet and RX resumes once the refills
succeed again.

Fixes: 1b9707e6f1a9 ("net: stmmac: enable RPS and RBU interrupts")
Cc: Russell King (Oracle) <rmk+kernel@armlinux.org.uk>
Cc: Nazim Amirul <muhammad.nazim.amirul.nazle.asmade@altera.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac4_dma.h | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac4_dma.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac4_dma.h
index 43b036d4e95b..d6c29b57bbf0 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac4_dma.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac4_dma.h
@@ -110,7 +110,6 @@ static inline u32 dma_chanx_base_addr(const struct dwmac4_addrs *addrs,
 
 #define DMA_CHAN_INTR_ABNORMAL		(DMA_CHAN_INTR_ENA_AIE | \
 					 DMA_CHAN_INTR_ENA_RPS | \
-					 DMA_CHAN_INTR_ENA_RBU | \
 					 DMA_CHAN_INTR_ENA_FBE)
 /* DMA default interrupt mask for 4.00 */
 #define DMA_CHAN_INTR_DEFAULT_MASK	(DMA_CHAN_INTR_NORMAL | \
@@ -122,7 +121,6 @@ static inline u32 dma_chanx_base_addr(const struct dwmac4_addrs *addrs,
 
 #define DMA_CHAN_INTR_ABNORMAL_4_10	(DMA_CHAN_INTR_ENA_AIE_4_10 | \
 					 DMA_CHAN_INTR_ENA_RPS | \
-					 DMA_CHAN_INTR_ENA_RBU | \
 					 DMA_CHAN_INTR_ENA_FBE)
 /* DMA default interrupt mask for 4.10a */
 #define DMA_CHAN_INTR_DEFAULT_MASK_4_10	(DMA_CHAN_INTR_NORMAL_4_10 | \
